# tools/s/sow_phase_witness.rish -- where a seed publish spends its minutes, read rather than recalled.
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/s/sow_phase_witness.rish
#
# WHAT IT STANDS OVER. tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_control.sh, which proves the scan from both
# sides in a throwaway pen holding a miniature field: a manifest with allow rows, a publisher, two
# drivers, and the projector they call. Thirty-three legs stand there, every refusal planted and
# then lifted, and five mutations are proven to bite -- dropping the comment filter on call sites,
# walking one hop instead of two, diffing churn without the allow pathspec, and keeping the vendor
# room in the candidate set.
#
# WHY THE INSTRUMENT EXISTS. REDS %642 books a content-keyed scrub cache, and the design that
# books it names what to measure BEFORE building one: how much of a publish is the per-file scrub,
# how much is the witness, and how many files actually change between publishes. A cache built
# ahead of that reading is a cache nobody sized.
#
# THE GATED READING IS STRUCTURAL, and it is the finding the measurement turned up.
# `publish-seed.sh` projects the whole seed once through `tools/s/sow.rish`, and
# `tools/s/sow_witness.rish` projects it AGAIN as its own duty 2 -- so a publish pays for two full
# projections and the second one is discarded. The witness has a sound reason: it reads `seed/`, an
# absent `seed/` reads clean, and its header says moving duty 3 ahead of duty 2 would turn it green
# over nothing at all. The reason was never in dispute; the COST was never a number. It is one now,
# held at a ceiling that only falls, so a third projection reds on the lap it arrives.
#
# COUNTED BY CALL SITE RATHER THAN BY RUN, because counting runs means running them and one run is
# six minutes on this pier. A call site is a live line naming the projector, reachable from the
# publisher in at most two hops. The scan's own header calls that a proxy and names both edges: a
# site inside a conditional still counts, and a projection reached at a third hop is invisible.
# Leg 16 plants exactly that third hop and asserts the scan does not see it, so the limit is
# measured rather than merely admitted.
#
# ONE ZERO WEARS TWO FACTS, and the reading says which. A churn span holding no commit at all
# resolves to HEAD and can only read zero changed; a busy span reads zero when the allow rooms
# genuinely stood still. `churn_quiet` tells them apart, planted as a PAIR in the pen, because
# either leg alone would pass under a scan that always answered the same word.
#
# THE SECONDS ARE NOT GATED AND NEVER WILL BE. `--time` runs a real projection and a real witness,
# twelve minutes together, and the numbers it prints are FREE -- nothing holds them still, and they
# rise as the tree grows. Read `20260916.120000` on this pier: projection 364.68s, witness 354.09s,
# of which the four proofs the witness actually performs cost 2.39s together. A number that free
# belongs in a page a reader can re-derive, never in a gate that would red on ordinary growth.
say "sow_phase: Language EN -- a publish measured before a cache is written for it."
say "sow_phase: Style Gauge Meter -- one gated structural count, the seconds reported and free."
say "sow_phase: Lens TAME -- safety first; the scan reads scripts and git history and projects nothing, so custody gate %1 is nowhere near it."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "sow_phase: the control must exit 0 -- every leg green in the pen (${control.err_brief})"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "sow_phase: a control that named no verdict has answered nothing"
assert control.out contains "legs=33" else "sow_phase: the pen's leg tally moved -- a leg written today must be heard today, never counted as a pass"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/s/sow_phase_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "sow_phase: the scan must run on this tree (${scan.err_brief})"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "sow_phase: a publish projects the whole seed more times than the ceiling allows -- read projection_sites above"

say "GREEN: sow_phase -- thirty-three legs proven in a throwaway pen, and this tree's publish closure projects the seed twice, at its declared ceiling"
